401
00:24:49,191 --> 00:24:52,404
without a video guiding every step.

402
00:24:52,404 --> 00:24:57,090
Use the relevant quiz and completion
certificate where available.

403
00:24:57,090 --> 00:25:02,001
Our Grade Twelve Mathematics study guide
is also there if

404
00:25:02,001 --> 00:25:05,490
you want more structured revision.

405
00:25:05,490 --> 00:25:10,177
In Lesson Six, we will move to surd
equations.

406
00:25:10,177 --> 00:25:15,088
Squaring both sides can give an answer
that looks correct

407
00:25:15,088 --> 00:25:17,809
but fails the original equation.

408
00:25:17,809 --> 00:25:22,721
There is a connection with today's
lesson: an algebraic result

409
00:25:22,721 --> 00:25:27,632
is only a valid solution when it
satisfies the original

410
00:25:27,632 --> 00:25:29,156
problem.

411
00:25:29,156 --> 00:25:32,369
Thank you for learning with me.

412
00:25:32,369 --> 00:25:36,564
I'm Chris, and this is Equation Station
SA.

413
00:25:36,564 --> 00:25:41,475
Recognise the structure, show the
mathematics, and always return to

414
00:25:41,475 --> 00:25:43,000
x.
